Author: GearUnclear <dane@danewagenhoffer.com>
Date:   Sun Oct 18 08:39:41 2026 -0700

    graphics: low-sun vehicles keep Classic's evening hue and readable shaded sides
    
    What the player sees: at a low sun the side of a vehicle turned away from
    it is no longer a dark grey shape. Its paint, stowage and markings read at
    about 0.6 of the sunlit side (M113 and Jeep 0.61 / 0.62 at a 12.7 degree
    sun, 0.57 / 0.61 at 7.5, 0.55 / 0.61 at 4.8; the Sinai Zelda and HMMWV
    0.60 / 0.63 at 12.2 and 0.56 / 0.59 at 7.6), where it was 0.41 to 0.49
    (Classic 0.33 to 0.53). The sunlit side of a hull takes the original's
    evening colour from 25 degrees of sun down, as Classic's own sunset ramp
    does: warmer than before in every measured box and at least as warm as
    Classic except two Jeep values, slightly less warm than Classic on one
    ratio each (lowsun_box r:b 1.26 against 1.28, dawn_box5 g:r 0.59 against
    0.58; the other ratio warmer). Golden-hour tree crowns lose their pale
    grey-green: the big broadleaf at forest_edge_golden comes down to
    Classic's brightness and reads greener, with the same light-to-dark
    spread inside the crown. The ground, its cast shadows and the noon frame
    keep their light.
    
    How it works:
    - lowSunRig (Graphics/Remaster/LightRig, ComputeLightRig): the sun takes a
      further LowSunHueShare of Classic's sunset hue over EveningSunChroma (0.4
      from 25 degrees down, 0.3 more below 9). The sun shafts take the rig's
      sun colour (the post pass's shaft tint), so the low-sun hue tints them
      too. Vertical faces get sideways fill below 40 degrees (LowSunFill: full
      from 8 degrees down to the horizon, faded out under it): the sky part of
      the anti-sun horizon times 1 + 2.6 fill, the sunward one 1 + 0.5 fill,
      the ground bounce 1 + 1.3 fill. The zenith term, the exposure meter and
      the sun's strength are untouched, so up-facing ground and its shadows
      keep their light; from 40 degrees up, and at night, the rig is unchanged
      to the bit. New: a limit on the fill for walls, the rule of the twilight
      cap but at every sun height the fill runs (-2 to 40 degrees), not only
      in twilight: the fill lifts a vertical face at most to the visible sky
      and never below its value without the fill (under a dim dusk sky the
      prototype lit a wall facing away from a 1 to 3 degree sun at 1.4 to 2.1
      times the visible sky; under a clear sky the limit does not bind).
    - crownCanopy (shadeRemastered, the research's crown V18 as plain code): the
      sun reaching a leaf crosses the crown in front of it (crownSunPath, the
      crown as a sphere, optical depth 1 per radius, a quarter always passes),
      the core sees 0.45 of the sky instead of 0.6, the leaf albedo deepens its
      saturation at equal luminance (a power of 1.3, renormalised), and below
      35 degrees of sun, fully below 12, the crown takes 0.65 of the sun and
      0.75 of the sky. Crowns only: grass (terrain draws) keeps its look.
    - The canopy flag rides in litHorizonSun.w (slot 23 had a free w): no
      LitConstants slot lands, the layout is unchanged.
    - Debug view 7 shows each lit surface's albedo (display space; the lit
      shaders see it as 4 through ShaderDebugView). With post=0 a shot of it
      divides a lit shot into the light on every surface: the research's
      calibration view, kept as the plan allowed (5 is the linear depth, 6
      A6's lights per tile; the lane, on 807ce4b, had it at 6).
    
    Switches and gates: lowSunRig and crownCanopy have landed (12/26 on the
    merged tree), both gated "always" (the rig is constants once a frame; the
    canopy is a few terms on foliage, and both fade themselves by sun
    height). The rig reads the switch (it runs before the gates, which take
    its cloud cover); the canopy flag comes from its gate. GPU section: world
    for both. Off (both 0) is the rig and the foliage of 807ce4b.
    
    From the prototype (tmp/research/shade): kept the hue share, the fill and
    its three factors, and V18 (canopy saturation, crown optical depth, core
    sky 0.45, low-sun crown sun 0.65 and sky 0.75). Rewritten: the moonlight
    1.01 sentinel became lowSunRig and the g_variant selector plain code under
    crownCanopy, ported onto F2's single crown normal and B1's leaf lift.
    Added: the limit on the fill, grass left out of the canopy. Dropped: the
    lazy vertex buffer (F8), the cloud floor (F4) and the in-scatter
    composite (F5), all landed as fixes; the debug-3 albedo hack became debug
    view 7.
    
    Cost: no GPU work of its own for the rig (constants); the canopy adds a
    sqrt, an exp and a pow per foliage fragment. One reading per view (S mode,
    1920x1080, 4x MSAA, scale 1.0, another lane's game on the machine, GPU
    clock not logged): frame minimum on minus off -0.41 to +0.35 ms over nine
    views with no consistent sign (the base build's own off and on, the same
    frame twice, spread -0.13 to +0.23 ms), so the reading does not resolve a
    cost. The full gate times it on a quiet GPU.
    
    Tests: test_remaster_lighting.cpp gains six cases: the shaded side of a
    hull readable with the rig (model of the research boxes' faces, 45 and 135
    degrees from the sun: 0.5 to 0.65, below 0.41 without, 4.8 to 14 degrees)
    and noon and night unchanged to the bit; the evening hue from 25 degrees
    and the lit face at least as warm as without the rig; lowSunRig=0 (and
    baseline) equal to 807ce4b's rig at 7.5, 12.7 and 30 degrees; the wall
    limit; the debug view mapping; the canopy's shader contract and its upload
    from the gate. test_feature_switches.cpp: shade landed (landed=10/26 on
    the lane), test_post_stages.cpp: the albedo view adds no post stage. The
    7 degree hue case did not move. The README calibration table is
    recomputed. On the lane, gate tags plus [FeatureSwitches], [FeatureGates],
    [PostStages], [SunShadows], [atmosphere], [triSetFixedStep],
    [triPinCloudDrift]: 529/529. Twelve mutations turn their cases red (switch
    ignored, fill or hue without the switch, no wall limit, hue from 35
    degrees, anti-sun fill 1.0, canopy ungated, canopy on grass, the stock
    core changed, canopy from the switch instead of the gate, albedo view
    unmapped, shade not landed).
    
    In game (tmp/integration/B2 of the graphics-remaster worktree): before
    (base build 807ce4b) and after sets of nine views (lowsun_fp, lowsun_box,
    dawn_box, dawn_box5, forest_edge_golden, noon_fields on Abel;
    sinai_lowsun_fp, sinai_box, sinai_dusk_box on Sinai with @LoBo), each shot
    classic, off, on and albedo in one game; measure_b2.md has the
    albedo-normalised boxes. Off equals before: the box values of off and of
    the base build are equal to 0.01 on every view, and the Abel views differ
    from the base build (a second boot) by the same kinds and sizes as the base
    build's own repeat within one game, in pixels over 2 levels: lowsun_fp
    40,918 against 43,969, lowsun_box 56,542 against 45,618, dawn_box5 45,159
    against 35,716, forest_edge_golden 148,132 against 147,872, noon_fields
    127,172 against 127,159, mostly in the horizon band, the largest on the
    posed soldier, whose pose differs between shots. Sinai's ground band
    differs between boots as A0 found, with equal means. smoke_abel 1/1 on the
    lane's final build, KHR_debug ids 131154, 131169 and 131218 only.
    
    Landed on B5 (e91b3f3; A6 and B5 landed after the lane's base, 807ce4b) by
    a three-way apply, 8 files in conflict, both sides kept: A6 took debug
    view 6 for the lights per tile, so the albedo view moved to 7
    (kDebugViewAlbedo; the lit shaders still see it as 4, their debug branch
    takes 1 to 4, and the backend passes 6 through itself beside
    ShaderDebugView); the comments of slots 22 and 23; the landed registry
    rows and their test (landed=12/26); the post-stage test over the debug
    views; the plan notes and the roadmap. Past the conflicts the canopy
    case's check of the debug mapping follows the merged line. Merged gate:
    build 0 warnings, touched files clang-format clean, the gate tags plus
    the landed lanes' tags ([FeatureSwitches], [FeatureGates], [PostStages],
    [SunShadows], [atmosphere], [triSetFixedStep], [triPinCloudDrift],
    [SeaWaves], [build-descriptor], [TemporalAA], [TerrainDetail],
    [FrameLights], [PerfCounters]) 577/577, smoke_abel 1/1 (KHR_debug ids
    131154, 131169 and 131218 only).
    
    Known risks: the M113 at 7.5 and 4.8 degrees (0.57, 0.55) and the Zelda at
    7.6 (0.56) sit 0.01 to 0.03 under the plan's 0.58 floor in these boxes;
    two Jeep values are slightly less warm than Classic (above); the conifers
    at golden hour are 9% darker than before and 15% darker than Classic (the
    big broadleaf is at Classic's brightness); the golden slope at
    forest_edge_golden reads more orange than Classic (r:b 1.60 against 1.39)
    and sunlit ground pinker (not mustard: its g:r falls); the fill is a flat
    lift on vertical faces, not bounce light; shaded hull faces are neutral
    where Classic's are bluish; the canopy also applies to the other half-lit
    shapes (bushes and, by the README, camouflage nets; the Sinai hero's net
    comes out brighter, 0.56 to 0.62 of its albedo, and the Abel hero's tent
    0.51 to 0.61, lifted by the fill); spawned vehicle sides at noon stay at
    the per-pixel level F8 made real (bounce is the lever). No RTX 3060
    measured.
    
